Subject: [PATCH] config.guess: name the elfsysvnt vendor

An ELF/SysV-on-NT system answers `uname -s` with `Linux`, deliberately and
permanently, so config.guess reading uname alone returns x86_64-pc-linux-gnu
and a native build silently configures for the wrong vendor. DR-0001 put the
project's name in the vendor field precisely because almost nothing reads it;
config.guess is the one thing that has to.

The compiler is asked, which is how config.guess already tells uclibc from
dietlibc from glibc a few lines above. A compilerless tree falls back to a
marker file the runtime installs, since config.guess does run where no
compiler exists.

Only the x86_64 Linux arm is touched. Other architectures keep their
hardcoded vendor, and a host without __ELFSYSVNT__ gets byte-identical output
to unpatched upstream, which the four cases in toolchain/config/README.md
check.

Against GNU config timestamp='2026-05-17', pinned in upstream.pin.
The five values this triple has to agree with are in doc/target-definition.md.

--- a/config.guess
+++ b/config.guess
@@ -193,6 +193,26 @@
 	if [ "$LIBC" = unknown ]; then
 		LIBC=gnu
 	fi
+
+	# The vendor field is the only place an ELF/SysV-on-NT system names
+	# itself, and uname cannot be asked: sysname is Linux there by design,
+	# so that the thousands of configure scripts branching on it keep
+	# working.  Ask the compiler instead, the same way LIBC is asked above.
+	VENDOR=
+	cat <<-EOF > "$dummy.c"
+	#if defined(__ELFSYSVNT__)
+	VENDOR=elfsysvnt
+	#endif
+	EOF
+	cc_set_vendor=`$CC_FOR_BUILD -E "$dummy.c" 2>/dev/null | grep '^VENDOR' | sed 's, ,,g'`
+	eval "$cc_set_vendor"
+
+	# Nothing above works without a compiler, and config.guess is run in
+	# trees that have none.  The runtime installs this file so that case
+	# still answers correctly.
+	if test -z "$VENDOR" && test -r /etc/elfsysvnt-release; then
+		VENDOR=elfsysvnt
+	fi
 	;;
 esac
 
@@ -1219,7 +1239,7 @@
 		x32) LIBCABI=${LIBC}x32 ;;
 	    esac
 	fi
-	GUESS=$CPU-pc-linux-$LIBCABI
+	GUESS=$CPU-${VENDOR:-pc}-linux-$LIBCABI
 	;;
     xtensa*:Linux:*:*)
 	GUESS=$UNAME_MACHINE-unknown-linux-$LIBC
